course: dictionary
lesson: 795
title: Words from the world of bees
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A beekeeper is a person who keeps bees in hives to collect honey and wax. Look at the word's parts: bee and keeper. A keeper looks after something, so a beekeeper looks after bees.
explain: Context shows you more. «In autumn the beekeeper lifts the hive to check its weight, to be sure the bees have enough food for winter.» Lifting a hive to check its weight tells you the beekeeper cares for the bees, not just owns them.
explain: Some words belong to one subject. In science and nature lessons, beekeeping is the work or hobby of looking after bees. Beekeepers wear a veil and a protective suit to stay safe, so the words suit and veil are clues too.
fact: A beekeeper keeps bees in hives to collect honey and wax.
fact: Beekeeping is the work or hobby of looking after bees.
fact: «In spring a beekeeper checks that the queen is laying by looking for tiny eggs like grains of rice.»
fact: Beekeepers wear a veil and a protective suit to stay safe.
fact: «A swarm hanging on a branch is usually calm, and a beekeeper can collect it.»
exercise: «In autumn the beekeeper lifts the hive to check its weight.» Why does the beekeeper do this? | To collect a swarm for a picnic | To make the bees sing | *To be sure the bees have enough food for winter | To find the queen bee's birthday
exercise: What does a beekeeper keep bees in? | Boxes of sand | Cages of glass | *Hives | Nests in trees only
exercise: «A swarm is the old queen with about half the workers looking for a new home.» Find and copy one word that means a group of bees leaving to find a new home. | home | queen | workers | *swarm
test: What does beekeeping mean? | Growing flowers in a garden | Catching fish in a river | Making cakes with honey | *The work or hobby of looking after bees
test: «The colony grows from about 10,000 to 50,000 or more by midsummer.» What is a colony here? | A type of flower | *A group of bees living together | A beekeeper's tool | A jar of honey
exam: «A beekeeper's year follows the bees.» Which job would a beekeeper most likely do in spring? | Sell bread in a shop | *Check the queen is laying by looking for tiny eggs | Read a book in the library | Skate on a frozen pond
